        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add /mark command for session label presets",
        "body": "Closes #(will create issue separately)\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nUsers want to visually tag their sessions with preset symbols (e.g. 🚧 in progress, ✅ done, 🔥 urgent) without manually editing session names. No built-in command exists for this.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds a `/mark` slash command that attaches a preset symbol prefix (separated by U+2800 braille blank) to the session label. Supports listing, setting by symbol/id/index/alias, clearing the mark, and switching reply language between Chinese and English. Uses the same session-store mutation patterns as `/name` and `/goal`, and only touches `label` + `updatedAt` (never `pinnedAt`).\n\n## User Impact\n\n- `/mark` → lists 6 presets (🚧 in progress, ✅ done, ⏸️ paused, 🔥 urgent, 📌 keep, 💡 idea) with bilingual labels\n- `/mark <symbol|id|index|alias>` → adds/replaces mark prefix\n- `/mark clear` → removes mark prefix, restores original label\n- `/mark english` / `/mark 中文` → switches reply language per session\n- Frontend autocomplete via `argsMenu: \"auto\"` and `choices` array\n- Presets loaded from workspace `mark-presets.json`\n\n## Evidence\n\nLocal smoke test (12/12 passed):\n\n```\n1. /mark list          → ✅ 6 presets + clear + english shown\n2. /mark 进行中          → ✅ label: 🚧⠀测试会话\n3. /mark 紧急 replace   → ✅ label: 🔥⠀测试会话\n4. /mark clear          → ✅ label restored: 测试会话\n5. /mark english        → ✅ reply language switched\n6. /mark list EN        → ✅ English reply text\n7. /mark 中文            → ✅ Chinese reply text restored\n8. /mark wip (alias)    → ✅ matched 进行中\n9. /mark 3 (index)      → ✅ matched 紧急\n10. /mark nonexistent   → ✅ proper error msg (CN/EN)\n11. pinnedAt preserved  → ✅ all 12 tests\n12. no duplicate reg    → ✅ single key/handler\n```\n\nFiles:\n- `src/auto-reply/reply/commands-mark.ts` — command handler (275 lines)\n- `src/auto-reply/reply/commands-handlers.runtime.ts` — handler registration\n- `src/auto-reply/commands-registry.shared.ts` — command definition + choices\n- `src/config/sessions/types.ts` — `markLanguage` field on SessionEntry",
        "branch": "feature/mark-command",
